===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=noun|:inh|enm:meeting<alt:meeting, meting><ety:inh<ang:mēting<id:meeting>><ang:ġemēting>>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|meeting}}, {{m|enm|meting}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mēting}}, {{m|ang|ġemēting|t=meeting, assembly, association, society}}, equivalent to {{af|en|meet|-ing|id2=gerund noun}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|moeting|t=meeting, encounter}}, {{cog|nl|ontmoeting|t=meeting, encounter}}, {{cog|gml|mö̂tinge|t=meeting}}. Compare also {{cog|nds-de|Möte|t=meeting, encounter}}, {{cog|da|møde|t=meeting, encounter}}, {{cog|sv|möte|t=meeting, encounter}}, {{cog|is|mót|t=meeting}}. Related to {{m|en|moot}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|[[gerund]]|uncountable}} The act of persons or things that [[meet]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Meeting''' him will be exciting.&emsp;I enjoy '''meeting''' new people.}}
# A [[gathering]] of persons for a purpose; an [[assembly]].
#: {{syn|en|powwow}}
#: {{ux|en|We need to have a '''meeting''' about that soon.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Jim Tankersley; Katie Rogers; Lisa Friedman|quotee=Joe Biden|title=With Methane and Forest Deals, Climate Summit Offers Hope After Gloomy Start|date=2021-11-02|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/02/world/europe/climate-summit-methane-forests.html|passage=Before he left Glasgow on Tuesday to return to Washington on a late-evening flight, Mr. Biden hailed progress on multiple fronts from the second day of '''meetings''' with heads of state, including initiatives to reduce emissions from agriculture.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220323192453/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/02/world/europe/climate-summit-methane-forests.html}}
# {{lb|en|collective}} The people at such a gathering.
#: {{ux|en|What has the '''meeting''' decided.}}
# An [[encounter]] between people, even accidental.
#: {{ux|en|They came together in a chance '''meeting''' on the way home from work.}}
# A place or instance of [[junction]] or intersection; a [[confluence]].
#: {{ux|en|Earthquakes occur at the '''meeting''' of tectonic plates.}}
# {{lb|en|rural|_|US|dated}} A [[religious]] service held by a charismatic [[preacher]] in small towns in the [[United States]].
#* {{RQ:Steinbeck Grapes of Wrath|page=20
|passage=You use ta give a good '''meetin''''. I recollect one time you give a whole sermon walkin' around on your hands, yellin' your head off.}}
# {{lb|en|Quakerism}} An administrative unit in the [[w:Religious Society of Friends|Religious Society of Friends]] (Quakers).
#: {{ux|en|Denver '''meeting''' is a part of Intermountain yearly '''meeting'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When "meeting" is used to mean a Quaker administrative group, it is often qualified by an indication of how often the group holds regular business meetings, such as "monthly meeting", "quarterly meeting", or "yearly meeting". When the qualifier is omitted, the term is assumed to mean [[monthly meeting]].

